# Trivy findings accepted with a documented reason. Keep this list short and
# justified — an unexplained entry here is how a real finding gets buried.

# DS-0002 — "Image user should not be 'root'".
# Both Dockerfile and addon/Dockerfile intentionally have no final USER
# instruction: the container must start as root to chown the Home
# Assistant-managed /data volume (whose ownership we don't control), then
# docker-entrypoint.sh drops to the unprivileged `app` user via gosu for every
# process — `exec $RUN_AS gunicorn`, so even PID 1 ends up as uid 1000. The CI
# smoke job asserts exactly that (`test "$uid" = "1000"` against
# /proc/1/status), so this is enforced, not merely intended.
# Same model as the HomeHoard/myMeal add-ons.
DS-0002
